{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"zone3_group","type":"group","x":5480,"y":0,"width":2720,"height":2340,"color":"6","label":"ZONE 3 · TOOLS & ISOLATION BOUNDARIES"},
		{"id":"zone2_group","type":"group","x":2780,"y":0,"width":2580,"height":2340,"color":"4","label":"ZONE 2 · EXECUTION & RUN LIFECYCLE"},
		{"id":"zone1_group","type":"group","x":0,"y":0,"width":2500,"height":2340,"color":"5","label":"ZONE 1 · CONTAINER & DATA HIERARCHY"},
		{"id":"title_banner","type":"text","text":"# Granite Architecture — Unified Master Canvas\n\nA bird's-eye architectural map of Granite v1 across three master visual zones: Container & Data Hierarchy, Execution & Run Lifecycle, and Tools & Isolation Boundaries.\n\n**Vault Specifications:**\n[[Start Here]] · [[Harness Design]] · [[Run Lifecycle Design]] · [[Memory & Context Policy]] · [[Repository & Context Tools]] · [[Tools & Permissions]]","x":2550,"y":-440,"width":2800,"height":320,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"zone1_container_rules","type":"text","text":"## Container Lifecycle & Storage Rules\n\n### 1. Cascading Deletion & Recovery\n- **Whole-Agent Deletion:**\n  - Moves intact agent directory into `agent-deletions/` staging.\n  - SQLite database deletion commits in a single transaction.\n  - Failed transaction restores folder intact; committed deletion stays deleted.\n  - Recovery scans restore uncommitted staged folders on startup.\n- **Container Deletion (Section / Project):**\n  - Settles and stops any active descendant runs.\n  - Physical internal directory tree is removed.\n  - **External Code Preservation:** Externally linked repository folders always survive deletion completely intact.\n\n### 2. Move & Reparenting Invariants\n- Permanent chats can move between projects in the same section, or across shared sections.\n- Closed section chats cannot be moved outside until the entire section transitions to Shared.\n- Temporary chats cannot be placed directly inside a repository project; user must first click `Keep`, then perform a repository move.\n\n### 3. File Editor & Safe Markdown Storage\n- Markdown files (`identity.md`, `memory.md`, `notes/*.md`) feature human live editing with revision-checking context publishers.\n- Optimistic locking: external edits detected immediately; saving during an active agent write is prevented to avoid data loss.","x":80,"y":80,"width":780,"height":2160,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"zone1_hierarchy_summary","type":"text","text":"## Containment Hierarchy\n\n```text\nAgent Container\n  ├── Section: General (always Shared)\n  └── Section: Custom (Shared | Closed)\n        ├── Project: Repository-Linked\n        │     └── Chat: Permanent\n        ├── Project: Chat-Only\n        │     └── Chat: Permanent\n        └── Chat: 1-Hour Temporary\n```\n\n- **Strict Tree Invariant:** All chats reside under a Section (directly or inside a Project).\n- **Physical vs Linked:** Internal folders delete with container; external linked repositories survive.","x":1020,"y":80,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"zone1_section_closed","type":"text","text":"## Section: Closed\nStrict confidential boundary.\n\n- **Zero Cross-Contamination:** Isolated from global agent notes and memories.\n- **Data Leak Prevention:** Cannot leak project facts, code, or context to other sections.\n- **Unidirectional Conversion:** Closed sections can transition to Shared, but Shared sections can never become Closed.\n- **Containment Lock:** Projects and chats cannot leave until the entire section is converted to Shared.","x":1020,"y":640,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"zone1_chat_temporary","type":"text","text":"## Chat: 1-Hour Temporary\nZero-footprint ephemeral session.\n\n- **Direct Parent:** Sits directly under a Section (never inside a repository project).\n- **60-Minute Expiry:** Countdown timer active only while idle; paused during active runs.\n- **Zero Memory Contamination:** Leaves no durable memory entries or search traces.\n- **Keep Action:** Promotes chat to Permanent, enabling subsequent move into a repo project.","x":1020,"y":1220,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"zone1_section_shared","type":"text","text":"## Section: Shared\nCollaborative, open context boundary.\n\n- **Shared Agent Memory:** Accesses global agent memories and notes.\n- **Built-in General Section:** The default `General` section is permanently Shared.\n- **Cross-Project Discovery:** Cross-project context retrieval permitted within section.\n- **Knowledge Contribution:** Insights and memories from chats contribute back to agent.","x":1780,"y":640,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"zone1_project_repo","type":"text","text":"## Project: Repository-Linked\nCodebase-backed development workspace.\n\n- **Codebase Access:** Links to external or internal repository folder on disk.\n- **Standing Permissions:** Grants standing repository read/write access to owning chats.\n- **Project Capacity Gate:** Exactly 1 active run permitted at a time across all project chats.\n- **Deletion Safety:** Deleting a project leaves external git directories completely untouched.","x":1780,"y":1220,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"zone1_chat_permanent","type":"text","text":"## Chat: Permanent\nDurable conversational stream.\n\n- **SQLite Persistence:** Persisted in SQLite database (`atlas.sqlite`) and logs.\n- **Connection Binding:** Bound to selected model connection upon first user prompt.\n- **Context Participation:** Contributes to conversation context & durable notes.\n- **Portability:** May be moved between sections/projects in the same agent.","x":1860,"y":1800,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"zone1_agent","type":"text","text":"## Agent Container\nRoot entity representing an autonomous assistant with dedicated personality and memory.\n\n- **Storage Root:** `application-data/agents/<stable-agent-id>/`\n- **identity.md:** Baseline persona, tone, and permanent system instructions (human-editable).\n- **memory.md:** Durable user facts, preferences, and project context.\n- **notes/:** Agent-level persistent knowledge, playbooks, and research findings.\n- **tools/:** Agent-local custom tools and executable scripts.","x":1780,"y":80,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"zone2_prompt","type":"text","text":"## 1 · Prompt Acceptance\nUser initiates an interaction turn.\n\n- **User Input:** Instructions + optional file attachments.\n- **Draft Preservation:** Composer keeps drafts and files locked until backend confirms acceptance into SQLite.\n- **Thread Binding:** Bound to target conversation thread in database.","x":2860,"y":80,"width":620,"height":400,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"zone3_context_notes","type":"text","text":"## Scoped Context & Notes\nCross-chat intelligence and memory isolation.\n\n- **Cross-Chat Retrieval:** `search_context` looks up relevant past discussions across permissible scopes.\n- **Closed Section Wall:** Zero context leakage; closed sections can never read or contribute to global notes.\n- **Memory Co-Authorship:** Human and agent collaborate on `memory.md` and `notes/*.md` using explicit save boundaries.\n- **Dynamic Compaction:** Context window monitored; completed large outputs pruned to save tokens.","x":5560,"y":80,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"zone3_skills_mcp","type":"text","text":"## Skills & Scoped MCP\nModular capabilities and external integrations.\n\n- **Agent Skills:** Instruction + tool bundles loaded from `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.\n- **Model Context Protocol (MCP):** Connects external tool servers over stdio or SSE.\n- **Precompiled Schemas:** MCP schemas compiled with Ajv on launch; defaults normalized before approval.\n- **Per-Section Binding:** MCP servers can be scoped to specific sections, preventing unauthorized exposure.","x":5560,"y":640,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"zone2_lifecycle_invariants","type":"text","text":"## Execution & Scheduling Invariants\n\n- **No Artificial Caps:** No hard limit on total steps or tool counts per run; termination is goal-driven.\n- **Worker Isolation:** Private utility worker (`src/backend/worker/`) executes SQLite, harness, and tools.\n- **Worker Deadlines:** 2-minute worker initialization timeout; 10-second graceful retirement window.\n- **Strict Determinism:** Messages and tool results strictly ordered and committed to SQLite before next action.","x":4500,"y":80,"width":680,"height":400,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"zone3_security_model","type":"text","text":"## Security & Boundary Defenses\n\n- **Renderer Sandboxing:** React UI has zero Node.js access; communicates solely through typed, validated IPC bridges.\n- **Secure Key Storage:** Model API keys encrypted via OS keychain (`safeStorage`); never leaked to renderer or saved in plaintext.\n- **Path Sanitization:** All file paths resolved and validated against container root to prevent directory traversal attacks (`../`).\n- **Process Group Cleanup:** Commands executed in dedicated process groups (`setpgid`), ensuring SIGKILL reaches all child processes on stop.","x":5560,"y":1320,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"zone2_stop_settle","type":"text","text":"## Safe Stop & Crash Settle\nGraceful cancellation and state preservation.\n\n- **Immediate Stop:** User clicks Stop → abort signal dispatched to active request and subprocesses.\n- **Edits Kept:** All completed file writes and git changes remain in place — **never rolled back**.\n- **Process Cleanup:** Active PTY terminals and MCP child processes terminated cleanly.\n- **Crash Settlement:** Unfinished tool calls marked interrupted; explicit user restart required.","x":4600,"y":640,"width":680,"height":420,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"zone2_failure_recovery","type":"text","text":"## Interruption & Recovery Matrix\n\n| Trigger Event | Harness Immediate Action | State Preserved & Guaranteed |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **User Stop Button** | Aborts active model request, cancels PTY process group | Completed file edits kept; pending approvals invalidated |\n| **Tool Execution Error** | Formats error result back to LLM context | Conversation intact; model reasons on how to recover |\n| **Context Window Limit** | Triggers native sliding-window compaction | Saved messages intact; older tool outputs summarized |\n| **Backend Worker Crash** | IPC client settles with error, marks run failed | Unfinished tool calls recorded as interrupted; no blind replay |\n| **App Quit / Window Close** | Startup recovery scans staged folders & active runs | Staged agent deletes reconciled; orphan locks released safely |","x":2860,"y":1800,"width":2200,"height":420,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"zone3_repo_access","type":"text","text":"## External Repository Access\nDirect filesystem interface for codebases.\n\n- **Standing Access:** Owning project chats read and edit files without per-line approval popups.\n- **Path Confinement:** Operations strictly jailed within repository root; symlinks outside are rejected.\n- **Deletion Independence:** Project removal in Granite never removes or alters the user's external git repository.\n- **Atomic Diff Tracking:** File modifications generate unified diffs with optimistic revision checks.","x":6320,"y":80,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"zone3_terminal_previews","type":"text","text":"## Terminal & Managed Previews\nNative execution engine and dev servers.\n\n- **Supervised PTY:** Confined terminal commands run via native PTY with real-time stdout/stderr streaming.\n- **Network Gating:** Outbound package downloads and network calls require authorization.\n- **Managed Previews:** Ephemeral dev server runner (Vite, Next.js) on isolated local ports.\n- **Automatic Teardown:** Previews cleanly terminate upon Stop, project deletion, or app quit.","x":6320,"y":640,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"zone3_isolation_matrix","type":"text","text":"## Summary: Three-Tier Isolation Architecture\n\n| Layer | Primary Responsibility | Isolation Mechanism | Failure Boundary |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Container Layer** | Agent, Section, Project, Chat | Directory hierarchy & SQLite metadata | Section confidentiality (Shared vs Closed) |\n| **2. Execution Layer** | Dual queues, streaming, tool loops | Single-project capacity & utility-worker IPC | Crash settlement & non-destructive Stop |\n| **3. Tool Boundary** | Filesystem, PTY, Previews, MCP | Path confinement, process groups, safeStorage | Subprocess termination & schema validation |","x":5560,"y":1800,"width":2320,"height":420,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"zone2_execution_outcome","type":"text","text":"## 6 · Outcome & Next Turn\nReconciliation and model re-invocation.\n\n- **Result Logging:** Tool execution results appended to chat history in SQLite.\n- **Context Fitting:** Fits context against model window budget; compacts older history if needed.\n- **Loop Continuity:** Harness invokes model for next turn or emits final response.","x":2820,"y":640,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"zone2_human_gate","type":"text","text":"## 5 · Human Approval & Questions\nInteractive human-in-the-loop gating.\n\n- **Approval Prompts:** Sensitive actions (code writes, shell commands, network access).\n- **Clarifying Questions:** Agent asks user questions via `ask_user_question`.\n- **Capacity Released:** Model slot freed while waiting for human input.\n- **Dispatch:** Approve → run tool; Deny → return error to model.","x":2820,"y":1220,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"zone3_tool_catalog","type":"text","text":"## Built-in Tool Roster\n\n### Repository & Filesystem\n- `read_file` — Read file contents within permissible bounds.\n- `write_file` / `edit_file` — Write or patch files with diff tracking.\n- `list_directory` — Explore directory tree structure.\n- `workspace_grep` — Fast deterministic text matching across permitted files.\n- `file_search` — Glob search for file patterns.\n\n### Context & Notes\n- `search_context` — Scope-aware search over chats and documentation.\n- `read_note` / `save_note` — Read and persist procedural agent notes.\n- `lookup_tools` — Discover available schemas and capabilities.\n\n### Terminal & Previews\n- `run_command` — Launch supervised shell commands in PTY.\n- `read_terminal` / `send_terminal_input` — Interactive shell I/O.\n- `kill_command` — Explicitly terminate background process.\n- `start_preview` / `stop_preview` — Manage background dev servers.\n\n### Human Interaction\n- `ask_user_question` — Structured interactive question prompts.","x":7280,"y":290,"width":800,"height":980,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"zone3_boundary_invariants","type":"text","text":"## Tool Dispatch Invariants\n\n- **Backend Enforcement:** Tool schemas in UI are advisory; the backend worker independently validates all arguments and permissions.\n- **Atomic File Writes:** Code changes write to temp files before replacing targets to prevent partial write corruption.\n- **Audit Logging:** Every command execution, exit code, and file modification is permanently recorded in the chat run log.\n- **No Blind Re-execution:** Stalled or timed-out tools report errors to model rather than silently repeating.","x":6320,"y":1320,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"zone3_future_v02","type":"text","text":"## Post-v1 Architectural Roadmap (v0.2)\n\n1. **Filesystem Chats & File Explorer:**\n   - Migrate chat storage from SQLite to JSON/log files directly in the filesystem tree.\n   - Built-in viewer for common files (`.txt`, `.md`, `.png`) in Granite.\n\n2. **External IDE Launch:**\n   - Clicking a repository opens preferred external IDEs (VS Code, Cursor, Zed, JetBrains) instead of an embedded IDE.\n\n3. **Isolated Worktrees & Repository Grants:**\n   - Git worktrees per chat for multi-run concurrency without dirty working-tree collisions.\n   - Same-section cross-project repository read/write grants.","x":7080,"y":1320,"width":800,"height":420,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"zone2_tool_loop","type":"text","text":"## 4 · Supervised Tool Loop\nSchema parsing & permission dispatch.\n\n- **Invocation Request:** Model emits structured tool call (file edit, command, search).\n- **Schema Validation:** Arguments strictly validated by Zod / Ajv schemas.\n- **Permission Evaluation:** Verifies container scope, section boundaries, and user settings.","x":3880,"y":1320,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"zone2_streaming","type":"text","text":"## 3 · Streaming & Live Steering\nProvisional token generation & dynamic input.\n\n- **Live Streaming:** Token deltas stream via IPC directly to renderer.\n- **Live Steering:** User sends steering message during active run; harness folds it into next cycle without resetting context.\n- **Connection Retry:** Bounded retry for transient HTTP errors before stream begins.","x":3800,"y":640,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"zone2_queue","type":"text","text":"## 2 · Dual-Gate Queueing\nConcurrency management across the app.\n\n- **Gate A (Connection Concurrency):** Enforces account/provider rate bounds.\n- **Gate B (Project Concurrency = 1):** Only one active run per project; successors queue cleanly.\n- **Settlement Ordering:** Successor run waits for predecessor to fully settle.","x":3800,"y":80,"width":620,"height":400,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"zone1_project_chatonly","type":"text","text":"## Project: Chat-Only\nConceptual & planning organization unit.\n\n- **No Attached Codebase:** Organizes multi-chat work without requiring a repository.\n- **Architectural Design:** Ideal for brainstorming, specs, prompts, and research.\n- **Upgrade Path:** Can be linked to a repository at any later point.\n- **Safe Scope:** Code-modification and terminal tools are disabled in this project.","x":920,"y":1800,"width":620,"height":420,"color":"5"}
	],
